              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ClassyUbe2791"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put the walnuts or pecans on top for those who don't like them. And i just use pimentoes because the children don't like olives. Crazy i know.",
            "datePublished": "2022-09-18T16:42:15.362Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "OLDWAZZY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making stuffed celery for years. I don't have a set recipe though. I just use your basic ingredients except no sour cream. I use a little of the olive juice to make it creamier. I always use two 8oz. packages of cream cheese and chop the olives , walnuts and add until it tastes right with enough olive juice to get the right consistency. Everyone always requests it for family get-togethers.\nThe filling is great on bagels and for sandwiches as well.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-06T13:19:52.683Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
