            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Martha Lutz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super convenient. I didn't have olives on hand but I had everything else and a jar of roasted red peppers to substitute for the olives. They worked out well but I will try the olives next time. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-21T00:44:52.458Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dollar Saver"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's easy and quick. I omitted the walnuts. Only because 1 family member cant eat nuts. I added twice as many olives. Made some for my lunch and snack for work.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-06T13:58:13.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "patioranch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "walnuts and green olives &amp; pimentos – who knew they would go together so well?! the walnuts add a very nice texture and different type of crunch to your stuffed celery. I made 2 batches: the first as the recipe was written which was very good. To the second batch I added 12-15 shakes of Frank’s hot sauce. I found this to be extra good with the sour cream and cream cheese mix. Both batches went quickly from the snack table!! Also, the recipe made as written makes a great spread for bagels (I suggest sesame).",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-10T05:43:04.597Z"
          },
